<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sergipe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sergipe is the smallest state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, on the north-eastern Atlantic coast between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahia">Bahia</a> and Alagoas, with its capital at Aracaju. The Portuguese conquered the area from its Indigenous inhabitants in 1590 and developed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> ranching and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> there. In the 1630s and 1640s it formed the southern edge of the territory controlled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Brazil.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sergipe.jpg" alt="Sergipe" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: E2m · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandeira_de_Sergipe.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
